- title "Neologin Cookie"
- use_responsive_design

:markdown
	The Neologin cookie lets us make authenticated requests to Neopets.com on
	behalf of our service account—mostly for `rake neopets:import`, which pulls
	Rainbow Pool data and Styling Studio styles. Neopets logs the cookie out
	pretty regularly, so we have to refresh it manually here when it stops
	working.

%section
	%h2 Current status

	- if @current_cookie.nil?
		%p ⚠️ No cookie has been saved yet. Paste one below to get started.
	- else
		%dl
			%dt Saved
			%dd
				= time_ago_in_words(@current_cookie.created_at)
				ago
				- if @current_cookie.created_by
					\— by #{@current_cookie.created_by.name}
			%dt Last successful use
			%dd
				- if @current_cookie.last_used_successfully_at
					= time_ago_in_words(@current_cookie.last_used_successfully_at)
					ago
				- else
					%em Never (no import has run yet with this cookie)
			%dt Status
			%dd
				- if @current_cookie.failing?
					🚨 <strong>Failing</strong> — last failure
					= time_ago_in_words(@current_cookie.last_failed_at)
					ago.
					- if @current_cookie.last_failure_message.present?
						%pre= @current_cookie.last_failure_message
				- elsif @current_cookie.last_used_successfully_at
					✅ Working
				- else
					🤷 Untested

%section
	%h2 Refresh the cookie

	:markdown
		**Service account credentials** (from environment variables, for staff
		convenience):

	%dl
		%dt Email
		%dd
			- if Neologin.service_account_email.present?
				%code= Neologin.service_account_email
			- else
				%em not set (NEOPETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL)
		%dt Password
		%dd
			- if Neologin.service_account_password.present?
				%code= Neologin.service_account_password
			- else
				%em not set (NEOPETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD)

	:markdown
		**How to extract a fresh cookie:**

		1. Log into [Neopets.com](https://www.neopets.com) using the credentials
		   above. (You'll have to solve their captcha—NeoPass doesn't currently
		   give us a way to automate this.)
		2. Open your browser's DevTools → **Application** (or **Storage**) →
		   **Cookies** → `https://www.neopets.com`.
		3. Find the cookie named `neologin` and copy its **Value**.
		4. Paste it into the box below and save. The next scheduled `rake
		   neopets:import` run will pick it up automatically.

	= form_with model: @new_cookie, url: admin_neologin_cookies_path do |f|
		= f.errors if f.respond_to?(:errors)
		- if @new_cookie.errors.any?
			%ul.errors
				- @new_cookie.errors.full_messages.each do |msg|
					%li= msg
		%p
			= f.label :cookie, "New neologin cookie value"
			%br
			= f.text_area :cookie, rows: 4, cols: 80, autofocus: true
		%p= f.submit "Save cookie"

%section
	%h2 History

	- if @history.any?
		%table
			%thead
				%tr
					%th Saved
					%th By
					%th Last success
					%th Last failure
			%tbody
				- @history.each do |c|
					%tr
						%td= c.created_at.to_fs(:long)
						%td= c.created_by&.name || "(unknown)"
						%td
							- if c.last_used_successfully_at
								= c.last_used_successfully_at.to_fs(:short)
							- else
								\—
						%td
							- if c.last_failed_at
								= c.last_failed_at.to_fs(:short)
							- else
								\—
	- else
		%p No cookies saved yet.